# Vision-Warning Banner — Front-End UX Pattern

Concrete CSS + HTML + JS for surfacing the "this model is text-only" warning
loudly with a one-click escape hatch. Pairs with `ollama-webchat` pitfall 14a.

## When to use

- Building a chat UI for Ollama / OpenAI-compatible models
- The backend `/api/models` already returns `vision: bool` per model (see
  ollama-webchat pitfall 1)
- The user has at least one vision-capable model installed

## The mistake to avoid

Rendering the warning as an 11px gray text node under the composer. Users miss
it. They attach an image, the model says "I didn't get any image", and they
think the app is broken. Three years of Open WebUI / Onyx / LM Studio have
trained users to expect a *visible* warning, not a quiet hint.

## The fix: full banner + capability badge + larger previews

### HTML

```html
<!-- inside #composer, above the existing composer-hint -->
<div id="visionBanner" class="vision-banner" hidden>
  <span class="ic">⚠</span>
  <span class="txt"><b>Text-only model.</b> Switch to a vision model to send images.</span>
  <button id="visionSwitchBtn" class="banner-btn">Use vision →</button>
  <button id="visionDismiss" class="banner-x" title="Dismiss">×</button>
</div>
```

### CSS (theme-aware via tokens)

```css
.vision-banner{
  max-width:820px;margin:10px auto 0;
  display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;
  padding:10px 14px;border-radius:var(--r-lg);
  background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--warn),color-mix(in srgb,var(--warn) 80%,transparent));
  color:#1a0f00;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,#1a0f00 30%,transparent);
  font-size:13px;font-weight:500;
