```

### JS — visibility + auto-pick + intercept attach click

```js
function bestVisionModel(){
  // prefer the same family as the active model (gemma4 → gemma4:12b, etc.)
  return state.models.find(m=>m.vision && /gemma/i.test(m.name))
      || state.models.find(m=>m.vision && /llama/i.test(m.name))
      || state.models.find(m=>m.vision);
}

function updateVisionHint(){
  const m = currentModelObj();
  const isTextOnly = !!(m && !m.vision);
  $('#visionBanner').hidden = !isTextOnly;
  $('#attachBtn').classList.toggle('dim', isTextOnly);
  // small dot next to the model name in the topbar
  const caps = $('#modelCaps');
  if (caps) {
    caps.innerHTML = m
      ? `<span class="cap ${m.vision?'on':''}" title="${m.vision?'supports images':'text-only'}">${m.vision?'👁':'·'}</span>`
      : '';
  }
}

// call this on boot AND every time the model changes
$('#visionSwitchBtn').onclick = () => {
  const v = bestVisionModel();
  if (!v) { toast('No vision-capable model installed. Try: ollama pull llama3.2-vision'); return; }
  $('#modelSelect').value = v.name;
  state.currentModel = v.name;
  updateVisionHint();
  toast('Switched to ' + v.name + ' — click "Load" to enable vision');
};
$('#visionDismiss').onclick = () => { $('#visionBanner').hidden = true; };

// intercept attach-file click when text-only — don't let the click fail silently
$('#attachBtn').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
  const m = currentModelObj();
  if (m && !m.vision) {
    e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
    $('#visionBanner').hidden = false;
    // re-trigger slide-down animation
    const b = $('#visionBanner');
    b.style.animation = 'none';
    void b.offsetWidth;
    b.style.animation = '';
    toast('This model is text-only. Click "Use vision" to switch.');
  }
});
```

## Subtle "design effects" that don't feel like noise

Pair the banner with a few additional touches that make the UI feel alive
without being annoying:

- **Slide-in for new messages**: 300ms `translateY(8px) → 0` on every newly
  appended message (user + assistant). Apply via `.enter` class at
  appendChild time; not on conversation load (which would re-animate 50 msgs).
- **Drag-over outline**: dashed accent outline + 10% tinted background on the
  composer row when files are dragged over. Removes on drop or dragleave.
- **Shimmer loading dot**: the `status-dot.loading` class replaces the
  default plain pulse with a 1.2s linear shimmer. More clearly "in progress"
  than a uniform pulse.
- **Pop-in for attach previews**: chips scale from `.7` to `1` over 250ms
  with a slight overshoot. The 90×90 size + accent border is itself the
  primary visual signal; the animation is a small confirmation.

## Pitfalls when implementing

1. **Don't animate on conversation load.** Apply `.enter` only when a message
   is appended by a `send()` / `edit()` action, not when rendering the history
   of an opened conversation. Re-animating 50 messages on open is jarring.
2. **Pick the closest family, not just the smallest model.** A user on
   `floki-k8` (gemma4 base) should be auto-routed to `gemma4:12b`, not
   `llava:7b`, because the response style will be more consistent. The
   `bestVisionModel()` function above does this in priority order.
3. **The banner must work even after dismiss.** Re-trigger the slideDown
   animation on the intercept-attach-click path (animation: none → reflow →
   animation: ''). Otherwise the banner reappears without motion and feels
   broken.
4. **Theme tokens only.** The banner background uses `var(--warn)`, the
   inverse text uses `#1a0f00` (a fixed dark for contrast against warn).
   Don't hardcode theme colors. All 5 themes (dark/light/terminal/brutalist/
   neobrutalist) carry a `--warn` token that's AA-contrasting.
5. **Don't double-fire the file picker.** The `e.preventDefault()` +
   `e.stopPropagation()` on the attach-click is what stops the hidden
   `<input type="file">` from also opening its native picker when the model
   is text-only.

